            <ArticleTitle>[The use of ultrasound at different frequencies in the treatment of patients with the neurological manifestations of osteochondrosis of the lumbar spine].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>30-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>85 patients with lumbar spine osteochondrosis associated with lumbar ischialgia and radiculopathy were examined and treated using high- or low-frequency ultrasound. Low-frequency ultrasound was found superior to high-frequency one primarily in patients with acute disease and concomitant spondylarthritis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
